catlass: mark __simd_vf__ member functions static for CANN 9.2.0

CANN 9.2.0's Bisheng compiler tightened the rule on
__attribute__((cce_simd_vf)): such a function must now be a free function or a
STATIC member function. catlass at the commit vllm-ascend releases/v0.27.1rc
pins (41bf90da655bba3c66d0acd7e00abe33960ecfd6) declares fourteen of them as
ordinary non-static members, so three ops fail to build against 9.2.0-beta.2 -
ChunkFwdO, ChunkGatedDeltaRuleFwdH and ChunkKdaFwd, the gated-delta-rule / KDA
linear-attention kernels:

  block_epilogue_fa_softmax_ascend950.hpp:329:5: error: simd_vf function
      'ComputeExpSubSum' must be a free function or static member function

The failure then surfaces as a misleading linker error, because the object was
never produced:

  ld.lld: error: cannot open .../kernel_meta/ChunkFwdO_..._mix_aic_0.o

This is upstream catlass commit c89fe73dbb68b65405675b80f89d6a451e3aab33
("针对VF函数补充`static`修饰"), backported. The pin is NOT simply moved forward
to pick that commit up, because upstream deleted include/catlass/debug.hpp
BEFORE it landed, and vllm-ascend at this ref still includes that header from
csrc/.../chunk_gated_delta_rule_fwd_h/op_kernel/arch35/gemm/kernel/gdn_fwd_h_kernel.hpp:16
- so no single catlass commit satisfies both. Backporting keeps every other
catlass API exactly as this vllm-ascend ref expects.

Only the in-class DECLARATIONS take `static`. The three out-of-class
definitions in block_epilogue_per_group_per_block.hpp (BlockEpilogue<...>::
AivPerTensor and ::AddBias, at column 0) must not, because C++ forbids the
storage-class specifier there - which is also what upstream's post-fix file
shows.

